     "explanation": "Stack-ranking is one of Sinek's clearest examples of a cortisol pump: it pits teammates against each other for finite ratings, breaking the Circle of Safety by design. The other three options are part of his prescription.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quiz: Not on the Diet</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spot the anti-pattern</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"240\" width=\"940\" height=\"120\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#ef4444\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" text-anchor=\"middle\">More stack-ranking</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pits teammates against each other → cortisol pump</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"450\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Decouple feedback from comp — yes</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"500\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reduce surprise reorgs — yes</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"600\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"650\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Specific, bounded threats — yes</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Stack-ranking is the canonical Sinek anti-pattern."
     }
