    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Cost of Doing Nothing",
     "content": "A subtle but important point: a leader who simply 'doesn't pump cortisol' is not yet leading. The default state of a modern organization is cortisol-positive — markets, news, social media, and incentive systems all push that way. To get to a Circle of Safety, the leader must actively COUNTERACT the ambient cortisol. Doing nothing means the team's baseline keeps rising. Leadership in Sinek's frame is a constant counter-force.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Cost of Doing Nothing</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Neutral is not safe</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#ef4444\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Default direction</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Markets, news, social media, incentives</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">all push cortisol UP</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"445\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\"I'm not bad\" isn't enough</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A leader who simply doesn't pump cortisol</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"535\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">still leaves the baseline drifting upward.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"600\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"645\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Active counter-force required</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Trust building must outpace ambient threat.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"735\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rituals, public sacrifices, specific reassurances.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">If the leader is neutral, the team is drifting.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Leadership is a counter-force — neutrality means losing ground."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quote",
     "title": "Closing Quote",
     "content": "Sinek writes: 'Layoffs and aggressive cost-cutting may save money in the short term, but they will cost us trust, loyalty, and innovation in the long term — currencies that take years to rebuild.' Lesson 5 examines what happens when this dynamic plays out across a large, dispersed organization: the abstraction problem.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Closing Quote</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Currencies that take years to rebuild</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"280\" width=\"940\" height=\"440\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"370\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">\"Layoffs and aggressive cost-cutting may</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">save money in the short term, but they will</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">cost us trust, loyalty, and innovation in</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"505\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">the long term — currencies that take years</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">to rebuild.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"650\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">— Simon Sinek</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Next: the abstraction problem at scale</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Trust, loyalty, and innovation are slow currencies."
     }
    }
